[
  {
    "text": "For any fixed wave vector k, evaluation of the quantum Fisher information F_Q[k] provides a valid lower bound on the entanglement depth of the system.",
    "topic": "lower bound per momentum"
  },
  {
    "text": "The full momentum-dependent QFI, as a function from the Brillouin zone to real numbers, contains strictly more information than a single scalar QFI value, thereby probing entanglement at different length scales.",
    "topic": "beyond scalar bound"
  },
  {
    "text": "The phrase 'goes beyond its role as a lower bound' and the characterization 'simultaneously provides a lower bound and serves as a momentum-resolved probe' are logically equivalent: the momentum resolution is an additional capability that does not negate the lower-bound role.",
    "topic": "compatibility and equivalence"
  },
  {
    "text": "In finite-size spin systems, the momentum-resolved QFI directly quantifies the degree of quantum entanglement at wave vector k, which manifests as a momentum-dependent entanglement depth and thus exemplifies both roles.",
    "topic": "finite-size confirmation"
  }
]
